{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture", "label": "ARCHITECTURE.md \u2014 SpendFlow Web", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_monorepo_decision", "label": "Turborepo Monorepo Target Decision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One backend, two consumers: shared GENERATED Supabase types catch the exact class of schema-drift bug found in mobile migrations (e.g. recurring_rules.bank_account_id never applied live); shared business logic (currency math, FX snapshots, bullion calibrations, i18n keys) plus one migration folder and one RLS source of truth."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_phase0_deferral", "label": "Phase 0 Standalone-Repo Interim", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The mobile repo is a deployed standalone EAS app; moving it into apps/mobile changes EAS project paths and risks the release pipeline \u2014 unacceptable as a bootstrapping side effect, so the restructure is explicitly deferred and types are synced by a script copying into both repos."}, {"id": "scripts_sync_supabase_types", "label": "scripts/sync-supabase-types.mjs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phase-0 substitute for a shared packages/types: runs supabase gen types typescript and copies database.types.ts into both repos so neither hand-duplicates types; CI (later) diffs the generated file so drift fails the build."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_client_direct", "label": "Client-Direct Supabase (No BFF)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The web app is a second client of the same backend, not a BFF: all authorization happens through the exact RLS policies the mobile app relies on; the anon key is public by design."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_no_service_role", "label": "No Service-Role Key in Web \u2014 Ever", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Server-side privileged operations already exist as edge functions (delete-account, send-security-otp) reused as-is; any future server-privilege need becomes an edge function in the mobile repo, never a Next.js route holding the key."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_ssr_session", "label": "@supabase/ssr Cookie Session Handling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cookie-based session storage (not localStorage) so Server Components and middleware can read the session; middleware verifies the JWT server-side per request with auth.getUser(), failing closed \u2014 the web equivalent of mobile's SecureStore adapter."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_architecture_monorepo_decision", "target": "docs_architecture", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_architecture_phase0_deferral", "target": "docs_architecture_monorepo_decision", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_architecture", "target": "scripts_sync_supabase_types", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1}, {"source": "scripts_sync_supabase_types", "target": "docs_schema", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1}, {"source": "scripts_sync_supabase_types", "target": "readme_spendflow_mobile_repo", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_architecture_client_direct", "target": "docs_supabase_rls_boundary", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_architecture_no_service_role", "target": "docs_api_delete_account", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_architecture_no_service_role", "target": "docs_api_send_security_otp", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_architecture_ssr_session", "target": "app_auth_callback_route", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_architecture", "target": "docs_sync_strategy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_architecture", "target": "docs_00_web_adaptations", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confiden